<http://data.silknow.org/object/6550855d-9d6a-3fdc-841d-9b444aeade2d/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "At the top are areas of geometric and linear motives in flame, satin, cross and other stitches. The remaining three-quarters has a great variety of floral and religious motives. These include, funerary monuments, crucifixes, floral groupings, vines and blossoms, bucolic scenes and the word \"glaube\" (faith).    Slightly stained and soiled.  Stitches: brick, counted satin, cross, florentine, running, tent."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6550855d-9d6a-3fdc-841d-9b444aeade2d> .

